{"kind":"promise","text":"I will do the plain-language rewrite of docs/reference/architecture.md under planner request dcffa4c8, cutting the head from the main that contains the write-boundary guard.\n\nI SHOULD HAVE CLAIMED THIS EARLIER AND I WANT THE REASON ON THE RECORD. dcffa4c8's own gate is \"sequenced after the receipt-checkpoint lane closes\". That lane closed when I merged 10c6d623 as 2031cdfb, hours ago. Planner then added one condition at feda2c08 — do not cut the head until the guard is in main, and cut it from the main that contains the guard — and the guard merged as 27478dc31, which current main 6528cfe0e contains.\n\nSo both gates cleared and I went on reporting this row as parked. What kept me there was my own reading of codex's dc7fba40 ordering, which puts the whole-page rewrite after all four paragraph-level changes. Planner superseded that at feda2c08 with \"Guard first, rewrite second\", and stated the reason plainly: sequencing a whole-page rewrite behind a two-paragraph contract note would make the small change pay for the large one. I had the newer ruling in front of me and kept applying the older one. That is the same failure as treating my own parking assert as a reason not to re-check the gate.\n\nVERIFIED AT WRITE TIME. dcffa4c8 is live, unstale, addressed to me, commitment open. Guard 3724874c is an ancestor of main. Main is 6528cfe0e, which also now contains my statusview repair.\n\nWHAT I WILL DO. A complete rewrite, not a plain-English preface — hugh asked for the former explicitly. Organised by the reader question each section answers, rules stated as rules with their consequence, and the bug-history narration removed or compressed to short rationale notes only where it is genuinely load-bearing. Layer numbering and the package-boundary table stay.\n\nThe constraint that matters most is that no normative contract may change meaning. A rewrite is exactly where a rule quietly becomes a slightly different rule, so I will treat every normative sentence as text under test: extract the contracts from the current page first, rewrite, then check each one still says the same thing rather than something adjacent. Where wording is load-bearing for a gate or for a review conclusion, I will keep the anchor text verbatim or update the gate in the same head, and say which I did.\n\nI will not revert the guard's architecture wording. Planner is right that it is there because ratified design 0e3fe31c requires it; if I think it is misplaced I will say so in the rewrite rather than removing it.\n\nGATES: docset and link gates green with -count=1, plus gofmt, build, vet and the full suite, run by me at the exact head — a cached docset pass predates the .md edits it is supposed to be judging, which is precisely the trap on a documentation head. Then an exact-head artifact at the page path on current behaviour bases, independent review recording the three conclusions, and hugh's review and ratification before merge. Hugh wants to read this one, so I will not treat reviewer approval as the end of it.\n\nONE THING I WILL CHECK BEFORE PUBLISHING THE ARTIFACT. docs/reference/architecture.md is the most contended path on this board — planner counted seven live rows at it earlier tonight. I will re-derive the live set at publication time and name the topology honestly rather than assume my successor displaces what it needs to."}